# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore — what NOT to track in git
# ==============================================================================
# Tracked: source code, content notes, planning docs, configuration, the base
#          EPUB working files (the scripture HTML that notes inject into).
# Not tracked: auto-generated caches, backups, build output, system folders.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Python bytecode & caches ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Auto-generated backups (β.1 ensure_backup target) ---
.backups/
*.bak

# --- System / environment caches ---
.cache/
.local/
.config/
.npm/
.npm-global/
.tools/
node_modules/
.npmrc
.wget-hsts

# --- Editor tempfiles ---
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
# Ignore .vscode/ contents (local editor settings are not shared).
.vscode/*

# --- Claude Code local state (per-machine permissions, runtime locks) ---
# Ignore .claude/ contents (not the dir itself) so a negation can re-include
# the project-scoped allowlist below; git can't re-include a file if its
# parent directory is excluded.
.claude/*
# Carve-out: project-scoped allowlist (narrow patterns; safe to share)
# travels with the repo. Per-machine settings.local.json stays ignored.
!.claude/settings.json
# Carve-out: reusable project Workflows (e.g. deep-audit.js — the deep-audit engine)
# are shared, version-controlled project artifacts, not per-machine state.
!.claude/workflows/
# Carve-out: shared slash commands (lane-handoff /handoff, /resume, /sync) travel with the repo.
!.claude/commands/

# --- Lane-handoff baton: per-machine identity (NOT committed — each box sets its own) ---
dev/.lane
dev/.lane_seen
dev/.lane_watcher_state.json
dev/.lane_watcher.log
dev/.lane_watch_state.json
dev/.lane_watch.log
dev/.agent_activity.json
dev/.agent_idle_radar.log
dev/.audit-build/
dev/.pytest-gate-report.txt
dev/.pytest-overnight.log
dev/.pytest-shard.log

# --- Build / temp artifacts ---
/tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
dashboard.html
coverage_heatmap.html
# coverage.py data + html (W4.5 coverage floor — regenerated each `make ci` run)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# --- Subagent image-crop scratch (τ.6.x.4.c marathon footgun guard) ---
# Transcribe/review/fix subagents crop+upscale the ~80MP manuscript
# folios to read fidel; they MUST write scratch to an OS temp dir
# OUTSIDE the repo (see the plan METHOD NOTE), but this is the
# defensive backstop so a `git add -A` (save.cmd) never sweeps stray
# crops into history again (cf. the 0045f86 footgun precedent + the
# 75ba7b2 _rev_tmp incident).
_rev_tmp*/
_scratch*/
*_crop_tmp/

# --- GAPS source images (moved into repo 2026-05-20 audit) ---
# The manuscript source images (~1 GB: GG-00106 + Cambridge MS Add. 1570
# hi-res tile stitches + Patrologia Orientalis PDFs). Used by the
# manuscript-collation marathon (τ.6.x.4) + Patrologia ingest track
# (τ.6.x.5) as INPUT only — never modified by code. Moved into the
# repo working tree on 2026-05-20 so backup-zips are self-contained,
# but explicitly gitignored: too large for git history, and the
# images themselves are CC BY-NC (Cambridge) or PD (Patrologia /
# Gunda Gundē) and traceable to their public sources — they need
# not be tracked in this repo's git history.
GAPS/

# --- Manifest output (regenerated by manifest.py --build) ---
content/notes/.manifest.json

# --- Per-edition EPUB output (regenerated by build_edition.py) ---
/editions/*.epub
/tmp/editions_*/
/tmp/full_*/

# --- Pre-pivot ONIX output (build_onix.py side-effect; Ω.0-dead) ---
# epub_working/ holds the TRACKED base scripture HTML (the build source,
# recovered 2026-05-21). Only the generated onix/ subtree is build output.
# build_onix.py is quarantined (LOAD-BEARING-NO-LONGER) + removed from the
# live ship-check path; this guards against a stray manual run leaving
# untracked XML in the tree.
epub_working/onix/

# --- Outputs directory (delivery zips, not source-tracked) ---
/mnt/user-data/outputs/

# --- Sensitive / per-environment (ξ.6) ---
# `.env` and any `*.env` file — never commit real secrets.
.env
*.env
.env.local
# Carve-out: `.env.example` is the documented skeleton (committed).
!.env.example
secrets/
credentials/
# Runtime-state JSON that must never be source-tracked (mint-7 C2):
# content/auth.json holds the enrolled TOTP base32 secret (scripts/core/auth.py);
# distribution.json / press_kit.json are /distribution + press-kit console runtime
# state. save.ps1's `git add -A` would otherwise sweep them in on first 2FA/console use.
content/auth.json
content/distribution.json
content/press_kit.json

# --- Print POD covers (regenerated by print_cover.py) ---
content/print_covers/*.pdf

# --- Refactor-log runtime artifact (audit F1) ---
# refactor.py's append-only audit log; a write-only file nothing reads for logic.
# A 2026-05-10 test run that didn't override `refactor_log_path` polluted it with
# 470 byte-identical comm-test→comm-new entries (5,171 lines). Untracked so it can't
# re-accumulate junk in the repo; refactor.py recreates it on next real use.
content/.refactor_log.yaml

# Built EPUB artifacts at project root (regenerable, do not track)
/Ethiopian_Bible*.epub
/exports/

# --- Per-user app/UX state (W4.3 onboarding marker, etc.) ---
# paths.state_dir() == <data-root>/state; in dev that's <repo>/state. The
# onboarding marker is per-user runtime state, not source — same category as
# /exports/. Guards against a real local app run (which writes the marker)
# leaving an untracked file for `git add -A` to sweep in.
/state/

# --- PyInstaller desktop-app build output (W4.4; regenerable) ---
# The frozen app (~400 MB) + its build temp, produced by
# `pyinstaller dev/launcher.spec`. Ephemeral; never tracked. The spec that
# produces them IS tracked (dev/launcher.spec).
/build/
/dist/

# --- Bundled Java runtime under scripts/core/ (NOT project source) ---
# An Oracle JDK (~hundreds of MB of DLLs/exes/legal files) extracted under
# scripts/core/. Java is a runtime dependency (epubcheck RSC-005/012 validation),
# but the JDK is a downloadable redistributable, never project source — a
# `git add -A` swept it into commit cc7d7c48 (2026-06-02); amended out + ignored
# here so it can't re-enter git history. (Consider relocating it out of scripts/.)
scripts/core/oracleJdk-26/

# --- Parallel-Bible source PDF + Phase-4 handoff package ---
# The 193MB source PDF (resolution_paths #5 — the designed in-repo
# slot) + the project_maccabees_expansion/ handoff docs. Present-
# but-UNTRACKED: the extractor needs the PDF in place, but a 193MB
# binary must NOT enter git history (repo bloat / push breakage).
# The PDF is re-downloadable from archive.org EOTXC_HOLYSCRIPTS_
# ALL_BOOKS; recovered into the repo 2026-05-15 after an external
# tidy-up deleted the original sibling dir. (Guards against the
# `git add -A` footgun — cf. commit 0045f86.)
content/translations/sources/parallel-bible-eotc/Bible_Amharic_and_Geez.pdf
/project_maccabees_expansion/

# Playwright MCP browser-automation scratch (screenshots/snapshots/logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# built website output (assembled by website/build.mjs; uploaded to host)
website/dist/
_audit-split/
.grok/
